From 0bc1b9dc800c81c6d49f6b53279f55879f2100fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:50:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(accounting): retire abandoned lease intervals [daveey]

Release discards the open token under the snapshot lock without recording a pass. A foreign-thread close retires its interval before refusing CPU booking, preserving existing no-pass semantics without leaking future unrelated CPU.

Proof: both independent reviewer cases RED on prior head; expanded five controls GREEN. Four exact-anchor mutants killed. Consumer run: 749 passed, 13 skipped, one exited-thread native-liveness assertion failed; unchanged residual suite rerun plus retirement tests passed with retries disabled. Full check found stale-base unrelated Desktop cap and synthetic OS marker; marker corrected, canonical ship rebase/check still required.
